  journal       = "arXiv [cs.HC]",
  abstract      = "Problem reframing is a designerly activity wherein
                   alternative perspectives are created to recast what a stated
                   design problem is about. Generating alternative problem
                   frames is challenging because it requires devising novel and
                   useful perspectives that fit the given problem context. Large
                   language models (LLMs) could assist this activity via their
                   generative capability. However, it is not clear whether they
                   can help designers produce high-quality frames. Therefore, we
                   asked if there are benefits to working with LLMs. To this
