  booktitle = "Human Behaviour in Design: Individuals, Teams, Tools",
  publisher = "Springer Berlin Heidelberg",
  address   = "Berlin, Heidelberg",
  pages     = "79--86",
  abstract  = "It is said, though not without controversy, that what
               distinguishes design from art is function. Design is for a
               purpose, usually a human one. As such, design entails both
               generating ideas and adapting those ideas to intended uses. This
               occurs iteratively. Form and function. Studying how people go
