  author   = "Hatchuel, Armand and Weil, Benoit and Le Masson, Pascal",
  journal  = "Research in Engineering Design",
  volume   =  24,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "147--163",
  abstract = "In this paper we present new propositions about the ontology of
              design and a clarification of its position in the general context
              of rationality and knowledge. We derive such ontology from a
              comparison between formal design theories developed in two
              different scientific fields: Engineering and Set theory. We first
              build on the evolution of design theories in engineering, where
              the quest for domain independence and “generativity” has led to
