  volume   =  17,
  number   =  4,
  pages    = "363--383",
  abstract = "Design educators often comment on the difficulties that result
              from a premature commitment by students to a solution to a design
              problem. Similarly practitioners can find it difficult to move
              away from an idea they have developed or precedents in a field. In
              the psychology of problem solving this effect is called functional
              fixedness or fixation. It is not surprising that these effects
