  number   =  5,
  pages    = "445--461",
  abstract = "This paper presents an approach for the integration of Virtual
              Reality (VR) and Computer-Aided Design (CAD). Our general goal is
              to develop a VR–CAD framework making possible intuitive and direct
              3D edition on CAD objects within Virtual Environments (VE). Such a
              framework can be applied to collaborative part design activities
              and to immersive project reviews. The cornerstone of our approach
              is a model that manages implicit editing of CAD objects. This
              model uses a naming technique of B-Rep components and a set of
              logical rules to provide straight access to the operators of
              Construction History Graphs (CHG). Another set of logical rules
