  volume    =  6,
  number    =  4,
  pages     = "505--529",
  abstract  = "Design practice is intrinsically about change and changing the
               world. Over the past two decades several new areas have emerged
               within design, such as service design, design thinking,
               speculative design, transition design and social design. What
               constitutes a desirable design outcome has also evolved. New
               design processes exist to enable those outcomes, and broader,
               more diverse communities often contribute to collective
               changemaking. Despite this, we still have a fragmented
               understanding of how to use design to create change, with a
