  number   =  4,
  pages    = "541--552",
  abstract = "Recent advances in artificial intelligence raise profound
              questions for humanity. Is the artificial intelligence-generated
              content (AIGC) technology merely a tool? Or is AIGC developing a
              level of creativity comparable to that of human beings? This essay
              explores the challenges and opportunities that AIGC technology
              brings to creativity, industry, and the ways of living of people
              around the world. These questions involve scale, authenticity,
              choice, and wisdom. Further, this essay addresses the core
              capabilities of future creative workers in the era of AIGC. The
              author believes that the ability to create meaning—meaning
              making—is and will remain a distinctive strength of human
              creativity in the AIGC era. To build on this strength, human
              beings must focus on six key areas: human-centered values,
              paradigmatic innovation, holistic experiences, cultural awareness,
              situational connections, and narrative reasoning. The best outcome
              for the AIGC is to make machines more machine-like and humans more
              human. Achieving this goal requires a cultural renaissance. We
              must break through the limits of computational rationality with
              the brilliance of humanity.",
  month    =  "1~" # dec,
  year     =  2023,
