  pages     = "1--17",
  abstract  = "ABSTRACTArtificial intelligence (AI) has breached creativity
               research. The advancements of creative AI systems dispute the
               common definitions of creativity that have traditionally focused
               on five elements: actor, process, outcome, domain, and space.
               Moreover, creative workers, such as scientists and artists,
               increasingly use AI in their creative processes, and the concept
               of co-creativity has emerged to describe blended human?AI
               creativity. These issues evoke the question of whether creativity
               requires redefinition in the era of AI. Currently, co-creativity
