               interdisciplinary research in the social and natural sciences.
               Nonlinear systems are ubiquitous; as mathematician Stanislaw Ulam
               observed, to speak of “nonlinear science” is like calling zoology
               the study of “nonelephant animals” (quoted in Campbell et al.
               1985 , p. 374). The initial phase of research on nonlinear
               systems focused on deterministic chaos, but more recent studies
               have investigated the properties of self-organizing systems or
               anti-chaos. For mathematicians and physicists, the biggest
