  number    =  3,
  pages     = "331--346",
  abstract  = "ABSTRACTA defining characteristic of service design is the use of
               external representations, which support designers in making
               intangible aspects of services accessible and shareable. Both
               current and future states are externally represented, using
               different service design techniques, for the purposes of
               articulating insights, learning, communicating, collaborating,
               and maintaining empathy for customers. The purposes of, and
               techniques for, making external representations were compared
