  number    =  2,
  pages     = "132--169",
  abstract  = "Diversity and mobility in education and work present a paramount
               challenge that needs better conceptualization in educational
               theory. This challenge has been addressed by educational scholars
               with the notion of boundaries, particularly by the concepts of
               boundary crossing and boundary objects. Although studies on
               boundary crossing and boundary objects emphasize that boundaries
               carry learning potential, it is not explicated in what way they
               do so. By reviewing this literature, this article offers an
