  journal  = "Frontiers in Human Dynamics",
  volume   =  4,
  abstract = "Recent advances in AI raise questions about its social impacts and
              implementation. In response, governments and public
              administrations seek to develop adequate governance frameworks to
              mitigate risks and maximize the potential of AI development and
              use. Such work largely deals with questions of how challenges and
              risks should be managed, which values and goals should be pursued,
              and through which institutional mechanisms and principles these
              goals could be achieved. In this paper, we conduct a systematic
