  volume   =  2,
  pages    =  8,
  abstract = "Assessing the influence of a scholar’s work is an important task
              for funding organizations, academic departments, and researchers.
              Common methods, such as measures of citation counts, can ignore
              much of the nuance and multidimensionality of scholarly influence.
              We present an approach for generating dynamic visualizations of
